Z||000002||Return of Fiero||10-24-2001||04:40 PM||||i could understand slowing down for puddles if they were about 8-10 inches or more. back in 95' i lived in raymond, and it flooded like crazy. never seen it like this, before, or since. anyway, on puddle was about15 Ft long, the width of the road, and about 2 ft deep in the middle. the side of the road was clost to 3 ft. (there was an escort on the side with water up to the window, thats about 3 ft, rhgt?) i slowed down sor the puddle, and once i was in, i floored it in first gear. the fiero was floating, spinnig, and i thought i was done. when the ass sunk in, it caught ground and hopped back up out of the water a bit, as well as forward. now if i put a fiero into that puddle, why cant an suv get in a 6 inch puddle?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spektrum-87GT||10-24-2001||04:56 PM||||i agree on a lot of the points you have stated... rain+speed=danger though, thats one time i wont even speed. but you're right, they should have stayed in the right line. One thing I've noticed though... the 'good drivers' are the ones that always do 10 over. It seems they always use they're signals, have consideration for other people, and stay in the appropriate lane. Those that do the speed limit or under usually dont use signals, stay in the left lane, and i've noticed they never use their mirrors. i've got a funny quote i heard a while ago. "isn't if funny that you think everyone going slower than you is an idiot, and everyone going faster is a maniac?" To clear something up, if people actually understood that the left lane is a PASSING lane, it would clear up a lot of traffic problems. If you've ever experienced that 'bliss' that is making it through the two slow people ahead of the pack, you know what i'm talking about. Shoot, if the driving/traffic gets too bad, me and a friend take both the left and right lane on a busy road and go 10-15 under, try this, its a stress reliever and a half! its kind of like revenge on idiots!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
